The rain stops in the evening, and a cool breeze blows.
I walk to the bus stop.
After five minutes, a BEST bus arrives.
I board the bus and find an empty window seat.
The bus conductor comes to me.
I say, "Brother, please give me one ticket."
He says, "Madam, the ticket is fifteen rupees."
I give him the money and take my ticket.
I look outside through the bus window.
These wet and shining streets look very beautiful.
I enjoy this monsoon evening.
Five months ago, I was very nervous on my first bus ride.
Then, that bus and those people were completely new to me.
But today I do not feel scared.
I know this route and all those stops.
Those days were difficult, but these days are good.
Now this city feels like my own home to me.
The bus moves forward quickly, and I smile.
